  <h1>Winter holidays with your dog</h1>
  <p class="guide-lead">Snow, snowshoe walks or just a stay in a chalet: the mountains in winter are very much something to share with your dog, as long as you know the resorts' rules and protect your companion from the cold. Here is everything Coco Explore has gathered to prepare your trip. The pages linked below are in French.</p>

  <h2>Good habits in the cold</h2>
  <p>Cold depending on size and coat, paws damaged by snow and salt, antifreeze, ice, cross-country ski tracks and national parks: our guide details the risks and simple actions, based on veterinary and official sources.</p>
  <p class="cat-see-more"><a href="/guide-hiver-neige-chien">Read the guide "Dogs in winter: cold, snow, mountains and good habits" (in French) →</a></p>

  <h2>Resorts where to find listings</h2>
  <p>For each resort, the dedicated page gathers dog-friendly accommodation, walks, vets and, when an official source exists, the essentials of local rules (leash, ski lifts, off-limits areas).</p>
