  <p>Going somewhere else? Find all the <a href="/hebergement-chien">accommodation that accepts dogs</a> and the <a href="/balade-chien">walks</a>, sorted by department (in French).</p>

  <h2>Rules in the mountains</h2>
  <p>Core areas of national parks, nature reserves, alpine pastures and livestock guardian dogs: the rules change from one massif to another. Our hiking guide takes stock, and the winter guide covers slopes and snow.</p>
  <p class="cat-see-more"><a href="/guide-randonnee-regles-chien">Read the guide "Hiking with your dog: where and when is it allowed?" (in French) →</a></p>

  <h2>On the road for the holidays</h2>
  <p>Most ski trips are made by car: what the law says, where to put your dog, breaks... it is all in our guide.</p>
  <p class="cat-see-more"><a href="/guide-voiture-chien">Read the guide "Travelling by car with your dog" (in French) →</a></p>
  <p>And in case of trouble on site, keep our guide to <a href="/guide-urgence-veterinaire-chien">finding an on-call vet on holiday</a> (in French) handy.</p>
